-- coa23-part35-delivery.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 35 (The registrar of companies), ss 1072 to 1079B,
-- lines 15080-15229 of ukpga-2006-46.txt: requirements for proper delivery, public notice of receipt of certain documents,
-- enhanced disclosure documents, the effect of failure to give public notice, and notice of documents about new directors.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING as in coa-definitions.l4 and the other coa23 modules (a "no" only
-- where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING for silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text,
-- limited by its own wording). Each branch that says no carries -- FALSE-kind (...); each "not covered" -- NOTHING-kind (...).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A bare "must" not done is JUST FALSE in a function named for compliance (fork F5).
-- Seam inputs are named as inputs/PLAN.md section 4 names them. Every top-level name begins with its section label.

§ `Part 35 - The registrar of companies: ss 1072 to 1079B`

§§ `s 1072 Requirements for proper delivery`

-- Every filing section in the Act asks this section's answer (inputs/PLAN.md section 4.2): the answer is the function below.
-- "is not properly delivered unless all the following requirements are met": the answer is the conjunction of the limbs, with a
-- limb that cannot be decided leaving the whole undecided, and a limb that fails making it a no.
GIVEN requirements IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1072(1) all the requirements in the list are met` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST FALSE) requirements
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document delivered to the registrar is not properly delivered unless all the following requirements are met" (an "unless" not met)
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING requirements
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on a provision, instrument or regulation outside the sources or in another part's range
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15082 | (1) A document delivered to the registrar is not properly delivered unless all the following requirements are met—
-- src:15083 | (a) the requirements of the provision under which the document is to be delivered to the registrar as regards—
-- src:15084 | (i) the contents of the document, and
-- src:15085 | (ii) form, authentication and manner of delivery;
-- src:15086 | (aa) any applicable requirements as regards who may deliver a document to the registrar;
-- src:15087 | (b) any applicable requirements under—
-- src:15088 | section 1068 (registrar's requirements as to form, authentication and manner of delivery),
-- src:15089 | section 1068A (rules requiring documents to be delivered together),
-- src:15091 | section 1070 (agreement for delivery by electronic means);
-- src:15092 | (c) any requirements of this Part as to the language in which the document is drawn up and delivered or as to its being accompanied on delivery by a certified translation into English;
-- src:15093 | (d) in so far as it consists of or includes names and addresses, any requirements of this Part as to permitted characters, letters or symbols or as to its being accompanied on delivery by a certificate as to the transliteration of any element;
-- src:15094 | (e) any applicable requirements under section 1111 (registrar's requirements as to certification or verification);
-- src:15095 | (f) any requirement of regulations under section 1082 (use of unique identifiers);
-- src:15096 | (g) any requirements as regards payment of a fee in respect of its receipt by the registrar.
@ref s 1072(1) Requirements for proper delivery (src:15082-15089 src:15091-15096)
GIVEN `the requirements of the provision under which the document is to be delivered as regards the contents of the document are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of that provision as regards form, authentication and manner of delivery are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicable requirements as regards who may deliver a document to the registrar are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicable requirements under section 1068 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable requirements under section 1068A are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable requirements under section 1070 are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1102 the requirements of this Part as to the language of the document and any certified translation are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1108 the requirements of this Part as to permitted characters and any certificate as to transliteration are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1111 the applicable requirements as to certification or verification are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of regulations under section 1082 (use of unique identifiers) are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements as regards payment of a fee in respect of its receipt by the registrar are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` MEANS
    `s 1072(1) all the requirements in the list are met`
        (LIST `the requirements of the provision under which the document is to be delivered as regards the contents of the document are met`
            , `the requirements of that provision as regards form, authentication and manner of delivery are met`
            , `the applicable requirements as regards who may deliver a document to the registrar are met`
            , JUST `the applicable requirements under section 1068 are met`
            , JUST `the applicable requirements under section 1068A are met`
            , JUST `the applicable requirements under section 1070 are met`
            , `s 1102 the requirements of this Part as to the language of the document and any certified translation are met`
            , `s 1108 the requirements of this Part as to permitted characters and any certificate as to transliteration are met`
            , `s 1111 the applicable requirements as to certification or verification are met`
            , `the requirements of regulations under section 1082 (use of unique identifiers) are met`
            , JUST `the requirements as regards payment of a fee in respect of its receipt by the registrar are met`)

-- src:15097 | (2) A document that is not properly delivered is treated for the purposes of the provision requiring or authorising it to be delivered as not having been delivered, subject to the provisions of section 1073 (power to accept documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery).
@ref s 1072(2) A document not properly delivered is treated as not having been delivered (src:15097)
GIVEN `the answer of section 1072 on whether the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has accepted the document under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1072(2) the document is treated as not having been delivered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of section 1072 on whether the document meets the requirements for proper delivery`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is about "A document that is not properly delivered"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the registrar has accepted the document under section 1073`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the provisions of section 1073 (power to accept documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery)"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the document is properly delivered turns on a limb outside the text

§§ `ss 1073 and 1073A Power to accept or reject a document`

-- src:15099 | (1) The registrar may accept (and register) a document that does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery.
@ref s 1073(1) The registrar may accept a document that does not comply (src:15099)
GIVEN `the document does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073(1) the registrar may accept and register the document` MEANS
    IF `the document does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document that does not comply with the requirements for proper delivery"

-- src:15100 | (2) A document accepted by the registrar under this section is treated as received by the registrar for the purposes of section 1077 (public notice of receipt of certain documents).
@ref s 1073(2) A document accepted under section 1073 is treated as received for section 1077 (src:15100)
GIVEN `the registrar accepted the document under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073(2) the document is treated as received by the registrar for the purposes of section 1077` MEANS
    IF `the registrar accepted the document under section 1073`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document accepted by the registrar under this section"

-- src:15101 | (3) No objection may be taken to the legal consequences of a document's being accepted (or registered) by the registrar under this section on the ground that the requirements for proper delivery were not met.
@ref s 1073(3) No objection to the legal consequences of acceptance on that ground (src:15101)
GIVEN `the registrar accepted or registered the document under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is to the legal consequences of the acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of the objection is that the requirements for proper delivery were not met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073(3) an objection may be taken on that ground` MEANS
    IF `the registrar accepted or registered the document under section 1073` AND `the objection is to the legal consequences of the acceptance` AND `the ground of the objection is that the requirements for proper delivery were not met`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No objection may be taken to the legal consequences of a document's being accepted (or registered) by the registrar under this section on the ground that the requirements for proper delivery were not met"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on that objection on that ground only (a prohibition limited by its own wording: marginal reading (b))

DECLARE `s 1073(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 1073(4)(a) the continuing obligation to comply with the requirements for proper delivery`
    `s 1073(4)(b) any liability for failure to comply with those requirements`
    `s 1073(4) another matter`

-- src:15102 | (4) The acceptance of a document by the registrar under this section does not affect—
-- src:15103 | (a) the continuing obligation to comply with the requirements for proper delivery, or
-- src:15104 | (b) subject as follows, any liability for failure to comply with those requirements.
@ref s 1073(4) What acceptance does not affect (src:15102-15104)
GIVEN m IS A `s 1073(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073(4) the acceptance of the document affects the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `s 1073(4)(a) the continuing obligation to comply with the requirements for proper delivery` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The acceptance of a document by the registrar under this section does not affect— (a) the continuing obligation to comply with the requirements for proper delivery"
    WHEN `s 1073(4)(b) any liability for failure to comply with those requirements` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) subject as follows, any liability for failure to comply with those requirements": subsections (5) and (6) then say when the period counts (fork F13)
    WHEN `s 1073(4) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two limbs are not closed with "only"

-- src:15105 | (5) For the purposes of—
-- src:15106 | (a) section 453 (civil penalty for failure to file accounts and reports), and
-- src:15107 | (b) any enactment imposing a daily default fine for failure to deliver the document,
-- src:15108 | the period after the document is accepted does not count as a period during which there is default in complying with the requirements for proper delivery.
-- src:15109 | (6) But if, subsequently—
-- src:15110 | (a) the registrar issues a notice under regulations under section 1094A(1) or any corresponding provision of any other enactment in respect of the document (notice of administrative removal from the register), and
-- src:15111 | (b) the requirements for proper delivery are not complied with before the end of the period of 14 days after the issue of that notice,
-- src:15112 | any subsequent period of default does count for the purposes of those provisions.
@ref s 1073(5) and (6) The period after acceptance, and when it counts again (src:15105-15112)
GIVEN `the provision is section 453 (civil penalty for failure to file accounts and reports) or an enactment imposing a daily default fine for failure to deliver the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the registrar accepted the document` IS A DATE
      `a notice was issued after the acceptance under regulations under section 1094A(1) or a corresponding provision of another enactment (notice of administrative removal from the register)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day that notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the requirements for proper delivery were complied with before the end of the period of 14 days after the issue of that notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073(5) the day counts as a day of default in complying with the requirements for proper delivery` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the provision is section 453 (civil penalty for failure to file accounts and reports) or an enactment imposing a daily default fine for failure to deliver the document`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for the purposes of "section 453" and "any enactment imposing a daily default fine"
    ELSE IF `the day in question` AT MOST `the day the registrar accepted the document`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) concerns "the period after the document is accepted"
         ELSE IF       `a notice was issued after the acceptance under regulations under section 1094A(1) or a corresponding provision of another enactment (notice of administrative removal from the register)`
                  AND  (NOT `the requirements for proper delivery were complied with before the end of the period of 14 days after the issue of that notice`)
                  AND  `the day in question` GREATER THAN (`the day that notice was issued` PLUS 14)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period after the document is accepted does not count as a period during which there is default in complying with the requirements for proper delivery", save as subsection (6) says "any subsequent period of default does count"

-- src:15114 | (1) The registrar may refuse to accept (and register) a document if—
-- src:15115 | (a) it appears to the registrar to be inconsistent with other information that is held by or available to the registrar, and
-- src:15116 | (b) in light of the inconsistency, the registrar has reasonable grounds to doubt whether it complies with any requirement as to its contents.
@ref s 1073A(1) The registrar may refuse a document for discrepancies (src:15114-15116)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar to be inconsistent with other information that is held by or available to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in light of the inconsistency the registrar has reasonable grounds to doubt whether it complies with any requirement as to its contents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073A(1) the registrar may refuse to accept and register the document` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the registrar to be inconsistent with other information that is held by or available to the registrar`
        AND  `in light of the inconsistency the registrar has reasonable grounds to doubt whether it complies with any requirement as to its contents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may refuse to accept (and register) a document if— (a) ... and (b) ...": a grant named "may", so a failed "if" is not the text's own "may not" (fork F28)

-- src:15117 | (2) A document is refused by giving notice of the refusal to the person by whom the document was delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 1073A(2) A document is refused by giving notice of the refusal (src:15117)
GIVEN `notice of the refusal has been given to the person by whom the document was delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073A(2) the document is refused` MEANS
    IF `notice of the refusal has been given to the person by whom the document was delivered to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document is refused by giving notice of the refusal" does not say it is refused only by that means

-- src:15118 | (3) A document that is refused by the registrar is treated for the purposes of any provision authorising or requiring its delivery as not having been delivered.
@ref s 1073A(3) A refused document is treated as not having been delivered (src:15118)
GIVEN `the document has been refused by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1073A(3) the document is treated as not having been delivered` MEANS
    IF `the document has been refused by the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document that is refused by the registrar"

§§ `s 1074 Documents containing unnecessary material`

-- src:15120 | (1) This section applies where a document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material.
@ref s 1074(1) This section applies where a document contains unnecessary material (src:15120)
GIVEN `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1074(1) this section applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material" (a failed "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:15121 | (2) “Unnecessary material” means material that—
-- src:15122 | (a) is not necessary in order to comply with an obligation under any enactment, and
-- src:15123 | (b) is not specifically authorised to be delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 1074(2) "Unnecessary material" (src:15121-15123)
GIVEN `the material is necessary in order to comply with an obligation under any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is specifically authorised to be delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1074(2) the material is unnecessary material` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the material is necessary in order to comply with an obligation under any enactment`) AND (NOT `the material is specifically authorised to be delivered to the registrar`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Unnecessary material” means material that— (a) is not necessary ..., and (b) is not specifically authorised to be delivered to the registrar"

-- src:15124 | (3) For this purpose an obligation to deliver a document of a particular description, or conforming to certain requirements, is regarded as not extending to anything that is not needed for a document of that description or, as the case may be, conforming to those requirements.
@ref s 1074(3) An obligation does not extend to what is not needed (src:15124)
GIVEN `the thing is needed for a document of that description or, as the case may be, conforming to those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1074(3) the obligation to deliver a document extends to the thing` MEANS
    IF `the thing is needed for a document of that description or, as the case may be, conforming to those requirements`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rule says only what the obligation is "regarded as not extending to"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an obligation to deliver a document of a particular description, or conforming to certain requirements, is regarded as not extending to anything that is not needed for a document of that description"

-- src:15125 | (4) If the unnecessary material cannot readily be separated from the rest of the document, the document is treated as not meeting the requirements for proper delivery.
@ref s 1074(4) Unnecessary material that cannot readily be separated (src:15125)
GIVEN `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1074(4) the document is treated as not meeting the requirements for proper delivery` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material" (a failed "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    ELSE IF `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the unnecessary material cannot readily be separated from the rest of the document, the document is treated as not meeting the requirements for proper delivery" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15126 | (5) If the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document, the registrar may register the document either—
-- src:15127 | (a) with the omission of the unnecessary material, or
-- src:15128 | (b) as delivered.
@ref s 1074(5) Unnecessary material that can readily be separated (src:15126-15128)
GIVEN `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1074(5) the registrar may register the document either with the omission of the unnecessary material or as delivered` MEANS
    IF `the document delivered to the registrar contains unnecessary material` AND `the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the unnecessary material can readily be separated from the rest of the document, the registrar may register the document either— (a) ... or (b) ...": a grant named "may", so a failed "if" is not the text's own "may not" (fork F29)

§§ `s 1076 Replacement of document not meeting requirements for proper delivery`

-- s 1075 is blank in this text.

DECLARE `s 1076(1) document that may be replaced` IS ONE OF
    `s 1076(1)(a) a document that did not comply with the requirements for proper delivery`
    `s 1076(1)(b) a document that contained unnecessary material (within the meaning of section 1074)`
    `s 1076(1) another document`

-- src:15132 | (1) The registrar may accept a replacement for a document previously delivered that—
-- src:15133 | (a) did not comply with the requirements for proper delivery, or
-- src:15134 | (b) contained unnecessary material (within the meaning of section 1074).
@ref s 1076(1) The registrar may accept a replacement (src:15132-15134)
GIVEN d IS A `s 1076(1) document that may be replaced`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1076(1) the registrar may accept a replacement for the document previously delivered` MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `s 1076(1)(a) a document that did not comply with the requirements for proper delivery` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1076(1)(b) a document that contained unnecessary material (within the meaning of section 1074)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1076(1) another document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a replacement for a document previously delivered that (a) ... or (b) ..."

-- src:15135 | (2) A replacement document must not be accepted unless the registrar is satisfied that it is delivered by—
-- src:15136 | (a) the person by whom the original document was delivered, or
-- src:15137 | (b) the company (or other body) to which the original document relates,
-- src:15138 | and that it complies with the requirements for proper delivery.
@ref s 1076(2) A replacement document must not be accepted unless (src:15135-15138)
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied that it is delivered by the person by whom the original document was delivered or by the company (or other body) to which the original document relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that it complies with the requirements for proper delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1076(2) the replacement document must not be accepted` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is satisfied that it is delivered by the person by whom the original document was delivered or by the company (or other body) to which the original document relates` AND `the registrar is satisfied that it complies with the requirements for proper delivery`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A replacement document must not be accepted unless the registrar is satisfied that it is delivered by— (a) ... or (b) ..., and that it complies with the requirements for proper delivery" (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1076(3) requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 1076(3) a requirement as to the identification of the original document`
    `s 1076(3) a requirement as to the delivery of the replacement in a form and manner enabling it to be associated with the original`
    `s 1076(3) another requirement`

-- src:15139 | (3) The power of the registrar to impose requirements as to the form and manner of delivery includes power to impose requirements as to the identification of the original document and the delivery of the replacement in a form and manner enabling it to be associated with the original.
@ref s 1076(3) The power to impose requirements includes power as to identification and association (src:15139)
GIVEN r IS A `s 1076(3) requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1076(3) the registrar's power to impose requirements as to form and manner of delivery includes power to impose the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `s 1076(3) another requirement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes power to impose requirements as to the identification of the original document and the delivery of the replacement"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15140 | (4) This section does not apply where the original document was delivered under Part 25 (company charges) (but see section 859M (rectification of register)).
