-- src:15146 | notice of the receipt by the registrar of any document that, on receipt, is an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078).
@ref s 1077(1) Public notice of receipt of certain documents (src:15143-15146)
GIVEN `s 1078 the document is an enhanced disclosure document on receipt` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1077(1) the registrar must cause notice of the receipt of the document to be published` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1078 the document is an enhanced disclosure document on receipt`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "any document that, on receipt, is an enhanced disclosure document"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the document is an enhanced disclosure document is section 1078 (above) and its inputs

@ref s 1077(1) The registrar has complied: published in the Gazette or in accordance with section 1116 (src:15143-15146)
GIVEN `the notice was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1116 the notice was published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1077(1) the registrar has complied by publishing the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice was published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1116 the notice was published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must cause to be published— (a) in the Gazette, or (b) in accordance with section 1116" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1116 is in another part's range (coa24)

-- The duty as a regulative rule (no time limit is stated). The recipient field is a placeholder.
@ref s 1077(1) The registrar must cause notice to be published (src:15143-15146)
`s 1077(1) the registrar's duty to publish notice of the receipt of an enhanced disclosure document` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Company, "publish notice of the receipt of the enhanced disclosure document"

-- src:15147 | (2) The notice must state the name and registered number of the company, the description of document and the date of receipt.
@ref s 1077(2) What the notice must state (src:15147)
GIVEN `the notice states the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the registered number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the description of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date of receipt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1077(2) the notice states what it must state` MEANS
    IF       `the notice states the name of the company`
        AND  `the notice states the registered number of the company`
        AND  `the notice states the description of the document`
        AND  `the notice states the date of receipt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state the name and registered number of the company, the description of document and the date of receipt" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

-- src:15148 | (3) The registrar is not required to cause notice of the receipt of a document to be published before the date of incorporation of the company to which the document relates.
@ref s 1077(3) No duty to publish before the date of incorporation (src:15148)
GIVEN `the day the notice would be published` IS A DATE
      `the date of incorporation of the company to which the document relates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1077(3) the registrar is required to cause notice of the receipt of the document to be published on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice would be published` BELOW `the date of incorporation of the company to which the document relates`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar is not required to cause notice of the receipt of a document to be published before the date of incorporation of the company to which the document relates"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that there is no requirement before the date of incorporation

-- src:15193 | (b) section 1077 (public notice of receipt of certain documents) applies as if the statement had been received by the registrar when the re-registration takes effect.
@ref s 1078(4)(b) Section 1077 applies as if the statement had been received on re-registration (src:15193)
GIVEN `a private company has re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the re-registration takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1078(4)(b) the day the last statement of capital is treated as received by the registrar for the purposes of section 1077` MEANS
    IF `a private company has re-registered as a public company`
    THEN JUST `the day the re-registration takes effect`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a private company re-registers as a public company"

DECLARE `s 1079(2) event` IS ONE OF
    `s 1079(2)(a) an amendment of the company's articles`
    `s 1079(2)(b) a change among the company's directors`
    `s 1079(2)(c) as regards service of any document on the company, a change of the company's registered office`
    `s 1079(2)(d) the making of a winding-up order in respect of the company`
    `s 1079(2)(e) the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up of the company`
    `s 1079(2) another event`

-- src:15202 | (2) The events to which this section applies are—
-- src:15203 | (a) an amendment of the company's articles,
-- src:15204 | (b) a change among the company's directors,
-- src:15205 | (c) (as regards service of any document on the company) a change of the company's registered office,
-- src:15206 | (d) the making of a winding-up order in respect of the company, or
-- src:15207 | (e) the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up of the company.
@ref s 1079(2) The events to which section 1079 applies (src:15202-15207)
GIVEN e IS A `s 1079(2) event`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079(2) the section applies to the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 1079(2) another event` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The events to which this section applies are— (a) ... (e) ..." (a list the text hands the definition to: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15199 | (1) A company is not entitled to rely against other persons on the happening of any event to which this section applies unless—
-- src:15200 | (a) the event has been officially notified at the material time, or
-- src:15201 | (b) the company shows that the person concerned knew of the event at the material time.
@ref s 1079(1) A company is not entitled to rely on an unnotified event (src:15199-15201)
GIVEN `the answer of section 1079(2) on whether the section applies to the event` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the event has been officially notified at the material time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company shows that the person concerned knew of the event at the material time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079(1) the company is barred from relying against the person on the happening of the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of section 1079(2) on whether the section applies to the event`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the event has been officially notified at the material time` OR `the company shows that the person concerned knew of the event at the material time`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not entitled to rely against other persons on the happening of any event to which this section applies unless— (a) the event has been officially notified at the material time, or (b) the company shows that the person concerned knew of the event at the material time" (an "unless" once met: fork F9)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "any event to which this section applies"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies to the event is not decided

-- src:15208 | (3) If the material time falls—
-- src:15209 | (a) on or before the 15th day after the date of official notification, or
-- src:15210 | (b) where the 15th day was not a working day, on or before the next day that was,
-- src:15211 | the company is not entitled to rely on the happening of the event as against a person who shows that he was unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event at that time.
@ref s 1079(3) Grace after official notification for a person unavoidably prevented from knowing (src:15208-15211)
GIVEN `the date of official notification` IS A DATE
      `the material time falls on the day` IS A DATE
      `the 15th day after the date of official notification was a working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the next day after that 15th day that was a working day` IS A DATE
      `the person shows that they were unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079(3) the company is barred from relying on the happening of the event against the person` MEANS
    IF `the material time falls on the day` AT MOST `s 1079(3) the last day of the grace period` `the date of official notification` `the 15th day after the date of official notification was a working day` `the next day after that 15th day that was a working day`
    THEN IF `the person shows that they were unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event at that time`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as against a person who shows that he was unavoidably prevented from knowing of the event at that time"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the material time falls— (a) on or before the 15th day after the date of official notification, or (b) where the 15th day was not a working day, on or before the next day that was" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

GIVEN `the date of official notification` IS A DATE
      `the 15th day after the date of official notification was a working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the next day after that 15th day that was a working day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1079(3) the last day of the grace period` MEANS
    IF `the 15th day after the date of official notification was a working day`
    THEN `the date of official notification` PLUS 15
    ELSE `the next day after that 15th day that was a working day`

DECLARE `s 1079(4) event` IS ONE OF
    `s 1079(4)(a) an amendment of the company's articles`
    `s 1079(4)(b) anything else stated in an enhanced disclosure document`
    `s 1079(4)(c) the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up`
    `s 1079(4) another event`

-- src:15212 | (4) “Official notification” means—
-- src:15213 | (a) in relation to an amendment of the company's articles, notification in accordance with section 1077 (public notice of receipt by registrar of certain documents) of the amendment and the amended text of the articles;
-- src:15214 | (b) in relation to anything else stated in an enhanced disclosure document, notification of that document in accordance with that section;
-- src:15215 | (c) in relation to the appointment of a liquidator in a voluntary winding up, notification of that event in accordance with section 109 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 95 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I.1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 1079(4) "Official notification" (src:15212-15215)
GIVEN e IS A `s 1079(4) event`
      `notification was given as the paragraph for the event requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079(4) the event has been officially notified` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 1079(4) another event` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Official notification” means— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." and the event is in none of the heads (a definition handed to a list: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    OTHERWISE
        IF `notification was given as the paragraph for the event requires`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Official notification” means— (a) in relation to an amendment of the company's articles, notification in accordance with section 1077 ... of the amendment and the amended text of the articles; (b) ... notification of that document in accordance with that section; (c) ... notification of that event in accordance with section 109 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 95 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989"

-- s 1079A is blank in this text.

§§ `s 1079B Duty to notify directors`

DECLARE `s 1079B(1) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1079B(1)(a) the statement of proposed officers required on formation of a company`
    `s 1079B(1)(b) notice under section 167G of a person having become a director of a company`
    `s 1079B(1) another document`

-- src:15220 | (1) This section applies whenever the registrar registers either of the following documents—
-- src:15221 | (a) the statement of proposed officers required on formation of a company, or
-- src:15222 | (b) notice under section 167G of a person having become a director of a company.
@ref s 1079B(1) This section applies whenever the registrar registers either document (src:15220-15222)
GIVEN d IS A `s 1079B(1) document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079B(1) this section applies to the registration of the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `s 1079B(1) another document` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies whenever the registrar registers either of the following documents" ("whenever" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b) and (c))
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:15223 | (2) As soon as reasonably practicable after registering the document, the registrar must notify—
-- src:15224 | (a) in the case of a statement of proposed officers, the person or each person named in the statement as a director of the company, or
-- src:15225 | (b) in the case of a notice under section 167G, the person named in the document as having become a director of the company.
@ref s 1079B(2) The registrar must notify the director or directors named (src:15223-15225)
GIVEN d IS A `s 1079B(1) document`
      `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as a director of the company, or in the notice under section 167G as having become a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079B(2) the registrar must notify the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is named in the statement of proposed officers as a director of the company, or in the notice under section 167G as having become a director`
    THEN CONSIDER d
         WHEN `s 1079B(1) another document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies whenever the registrar registers either of the following documents"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person or each person named in the statement as a director of the company" and "the person named in the document as having become a director"

@ref s 1079B(2) The registrar has notified the person as the section requires (src:15223-15225)
GIVEN `the registrar has notified the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it did so as soon as reasonably practicable after registering the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079B(2) the registrar has notified the person as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has notified the person` AND `it did so as soon as reasonably practicable after registering the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As soon as reasonably practicable after registering the document, the registrar must notify" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

-- The duty as a regulative rule. "As soon as reasonably practicable" is a standard and not a number of days, so the rule has no WITHIN.
@ref s 1079B(2) The registrar must notify the person (src:15223-15225)
`s 1079B(2) the registrar's duty to notify the person named as a director` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Director, "notify the person named in the document as a director of the company"

-- src:15226 | (3) The notice must—
-- src:15227 | (a) state that the person is named in the document as a director of the company, and
-- src:15228 | (b) include such information relating to the office and duties of a director (or such details of where information of that sort can be found) as the Secretary of State may from time to time direct the registrar to include.
@ref s 1079B(3) What the notice must contain (src:15226-15228)
GIVEN `the notice states that the person is named in the document as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes the information relating to the office and duties of a director, or the details of where it can be found, that the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to include` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079B(3) the notice contains what it must` MEANS
    IF `the notice states that the person is named in the document as a director of the company` AND `the notice includes the information relating to the office and duties of a director, or the details of where it can be found, that the Secretary of State has directed the registrar to include`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must— (a) state that the person is named in the document as a director of the company, and (b) include such information relating to the office and duties of a director" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

-- src:15229 | (4) The notice may be sent in hard copy or electronic form to any address for the person that the registrar has received from either the subscribers or the company.
@ref s 1079B(4) The form of the notice and the address (src:15229)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the address is one the registrar has received from either the subscribers or the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1079B(4) the notice may be sent in the form to the address` MEANS
    IF `the address is one the registrar has received from either the subscribers or the company`
    THEN CONSIDER form
         WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any address for the person that the registrar has received from either the subscribers or the company"
